Here is an example of the complete configuration for the `index.ts` file (in the `src/migrations` folder) and the `package.json` file:

*`src/migrations/index.ts`*
```
import { MigrationInterface, QueryRunner } from 'typeorm';
import { createConnection } from 'typeorm';

createConnection({
  type: 'postgres',
  url: 'localhost:5432',
  username: 'postgres',
  password: 'password',
  database: 'omr_exam_db',
  entities: ['src/entities/**/*.ts'],
  migrations: ['src/migrations/**/*.ts'],
});

export class MigrationRunner implements MigrationInterface {
  async up(queryRunner: QueryRunner): Promise<void> {
    // Apply migrations here
  }

  async down(queryRunner: QueryRunner): Promise<void> {
    // Revert migrations here
  }
}
```
*`package.json`*
```
{
  "name": "omr-exam-db",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "scripts": {
    "migrate": "ts-node src/migrations/index.ts",
    "migrate:up": "ts-node src/migrations/index.ts up",
    "migrate:down": "ts-node src/migrations/index.ts down"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "typeorm": "^0.2.34",
    "pg": "^8.5.1",
    "ts-node": "^10.2.1"
  }
}
```
With this configuration, you can run the migrations using the following commands:

- `npm run migrate` (to run all migrations)
- `npm run migrate:up` (to run all migrations in the "up" direction)
- `npm run migrate:down` (to run all migrations in the "down" direction)

Make sure to adjust the database connection settings in the `index.ts` file to match your PostgreSQL database credentials.

Also, make sure to install the required dependencies by running `npm install` in your project directory.

If you're still having issues running migrations, please provide more details about the error message you're seeing, and I'll do my best to help you troubleshoot.
